-- CONTROL for #1599. Same six modules, same graph, ONE variable changed: the goal
-- `Show2 (Box T)` is posed HERE, in an entry that imports `spec`, instead of inside
-- `user.mdk`, which does not. So the more-specific `impl Show2 (Box T)` is reachable
-- from the module posing the goal and most-specific-wins can actually apply.
--
-- Correct answer 5, and the control asserts the compiler gets it: if this ever stops
-- printing 5, the bug is no longer "an unreachable specific impl loses" but something
-- broader, and #1599's main.mdk would be pinning the wrong thing.
